%N A398585 Decimal expansion of Re(Li_3(1 + i)), where Li_3(z) is the polylogarithm function of order 3, and i is the imaginary unit.
%H A398585 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 6.53, p. 774, eq. (6.405).
%H A398585 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polylogarithm">Polylogarithm</a>.
%H A398585 Ming Hao Zhao, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.12155">On logarithmic integrals, harmonic sums and variations</a>, arXiv:1911.12155 [math.CA], 2019-2020. See section 5.3, p. 36.
%F A398585 Equals Re(Li_3(1 - i)).
%F A398585 Equals 35*zeta(3)/64 + 3*log(2)*zeta(2)/16.
%e A398585 0.871158883410938016854465530637639715927719973879582...
%t A398585 RealDigits[Re[PolyLog[3, 1+I]], 10, 120][[1]]
%t A398585 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398585 RealDigits[35*Zeta[3]/64 + 3*Log[2]*Zeta[2]/16, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398585 (PARI) real(polylog(3, 1+I))
%o A398585 (PARI) 35*zeta(3)/64 + 3*log(2)*zeta(2)/16
%Y A398585 Cf. A002117, A002162, A013661, A398586.
%Y A398585 Re(Li_k(1 + i)): A222068 (k=2), this constant (k=3), A398587 (k=4).
